window.DIGEST.foryou.push(...[{"id": "2112698374172610903", "url": "https://x.com/radixark/status/2112698374172610903", "text": "Beam × Miles 🤝\nWe've published RL post-training recipes for @reflection_ai's Beam, covering full-parameter GRPO and LoRA training with SGLang-powered rollouts.\n\nThanks @chetantekur and the Reflection team for the collaboration!\n\nCheck out the cookbook: https://miles.radixark.com/docs/models/reflection/beam", "name": "RadixArk", "handle": "radixark", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1996396384120086528/UzE4Waox_200x200.jpg", "likes": 33, "rts": 3, "replies": 0, "views": 2093, "ts": 1792541519, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112691846308876402", "url": "https://x.com/chetantekur/status/2112691846308876402", "text": "We have been working on making Beam easier to customize at @reflection_ai. Seeing the recipes and integrations go live feels pretty amazing.\n\nWe're putting the code, training configs, and examples out there so people can start building on Beam. Here's what's in the cookbook:\n\nData generation: Use Beam to create training data, including software-engineering trajectories that pass tests and reasoning examples for tool calling.\nhttps://github.com/reflection-oss/cookbook/tree/main/recipes/customization/data-synthesis\n\nFine-tuning: Adapt Beam to your data and tasks with LoRA, QLoRA, or full fine-tuning.\nhttps://github.com/reflection-oss/cookbook/tree/main/recipes/customization/sft\n\nDistillation: Use Beam to teach a smaller model. We've included recipes for coding trajectories and tool-calling reasoning.\nCoding: https://github.com/reflection-oss/cookbook/tree/main/recipes/customization/sft/distil-swe-agent\nTool calling: https://github.com/reflection-oss/cookbook/tree/main/recipes/customization/sft/reasoning-distillation\n\nReinforcement learning: Post-train Beam against verifiable rewards.\nhttps://github.com/reflection-oss/cookbook/tree/main/recipes/customization/rl\n\nHuge thanks to our partners and the teams behind these integrations:\n\n• NeMo AutoModel, @NVIDIAAIDev: SFT with LoRA and full fine-tuning.\nhttps://docs.nvidia.com/nemo/automodel/nightly/model-coverage/large-language-models/reflection/Beam-1.0-501B-A23B\n\n• Megatron Bridge, @NVIDIAAIDev: Large-scale full fine-tuning.\nhttps://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge/tree/main/examples/models/beam\n\n• Axolotl, @axolotl_ai: LoRA, QLoRA, and full fine-tuning.\nhttps://github.com/axolotl-ai-cloud/axolotl/tree/main/examples/beam\n\n• HF TRL, @huggingface: Training smaller models on Beam-generated data.\nhttps://github.com/huggingface/trl\n\n• Miles, @radixark: RL post-training.\nhttps://miles.radixark.com/docs/models/reflection/beam\n\n• NeMo RL, @NVIDIAAIDev: RL post-training on NVIDIA hardware.\nhttps://github.com/NVIDIA-NeMo/RL/blob/beam-support/docs/guides/models/reflection/beam.md\n\n• SkyRL, @NovaSkyAI: LoRA and full-parameter RL.\nhttps://docs.skyrl.ai/docs/examples/beam\n\nEach recipe has its own instructions, dependencies, sample inputs, and smoke test. I'm excited to see people run these experiments, adapt Beam to their own work, and contribute recipes we haven't thought of.\n\nHuge thanks to @Nazeri2010, @bhutanisanyam1, @kathleen_mhatre, @FGbelidji, @joespeez, and to Thibaut, Matthias, Travis, Kai, and Yoni for making this happen.\n\nExplore the cookbook: https://github.com/reflection-oss/cookbook\n\nAccess the model: https://platform.reflection.ai\nDocumentation: https://developers.reflection.ai\nProvide feedback on Discord: https://discord.com/invite/PxUfdsNny", "name": "Chetan Tekur", "handle": "chetantekur", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2018577161163276288/u_6GcQpw_200x200.jpg", "likes": 47, "rts": 6, "replies": 2, "views": 3464, "ts": 1792539962, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.22, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112533204112642519", "url": "https://x.com/haider1/status/2112533204112642519", "text": "if i were at openai i'd be planning one decisive model response to both opus and fable 5.5 rather than another cost-focused model\n\ntake your time, but release something that doesn't just reclaim the intelligence lead but also wins on speed, cost and especially efficiency\n\nnow imagine dropping that model right around anthropic's IPO", "name": "Haider.", "handle": "haider1", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2047286007003848704/u2mzg86I_200x200.jpg", "likes": 46, "rts": 3, "replies": 7, "views": 4036, "ts": 1792502139, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.21, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112607122319876268", "url": "https://x.com/NaoXprotocol/status/2112607122319876268", "text": "Unpopular opinion: crypto agility is a bit of a fantasy 🦄\n\nIt's becoming a real buzzword across the industry right now. But is it actually a smart move?\n\nPeople don't build cryptography. They build applications, and the crypto has to fit whatever limits the app sets.\n\nThe cryptography team at @HorizenLabs explain👇", "name": "NaoX | Post-Quantum Chain", "handle": "NaoXprotocol", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2078199106665693184/KA-t1xcf_200x200.jpg", "likes": 35, "rts": 4, "replies": 4, "views": 2761, "ts": 1792519762, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112607091789570048/pu/vid/avc1/640x360/B3ySXfTIi8FrY2NB.mp4?tag=12", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112607091789570048/pu/vid/avc1/1280x720/OzB5hsnRGUNQxwhP.mp4?tag=12", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2112607091789570048/pu/img/5F3PrAqq5XcocgIO.jpg", "dur": 75}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.21, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112533429698932938", "url": "https://x.com/ftcarpe/status/2112533429698932938", "text": "Natural language is an unusual interface. people speak in fragments, leave out context, and often figure out what they mean while explaining it.\n\nSpeakON makes that interaction worth examining by pairing voice input with a personal agent. the interesting question is how well that approach handles the gap between expressing an intention and taking the next step.", "name": "carpe", "handle": "ftcarpe", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2100922371536502784/mtPoXt0r_200x200.jpg", "likes": 58, "rts": 3, "replies": 1, "views": 15522, "ts": 1792502193, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112529279468835313", "url": "https://x.com/SpeakON_Global/status/2112529279468835313", "text": "we crushed a keyboard.\nits retirement party got a little out of hand.\n\nfor years, it was there for every email, every plan, every “just one more thing.” a loyal colleague. a very loud colleague.\n\nbut your ideas move faster than your fingers.\nand somewhere between knowing what you want to do and typing it all out, a quick task becomes another thing taking up your afternoon.\n\nmeet SpeakON AI Agent.\nstart with what you need, in your own words. less time behind a blinking cursor. more room to move things forward.\n\nthe keyboard had a good run.\nnow, let’s give your voice a turn.\n\nTHE LAST KEYSTROKE is here. watch the film, then tell us: what’s the first task you’d hand over?\nhttps://www.speakon.app/x\n\nDisclaimer: The calling feature is still in beta and will be available soon. All other Agent features are available now, with ongoing improvements.", "name": "SpeakON", "handle": "SpeakON_Global", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2034517364835004416/t7JRTf-G_200x200.jpg", "likes": 360, "rts": 27, "replies": 132, "views": 1088380, "ts": 1792501203, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112515374826541056/vid/avc1/1280x720/1pVCcXx5_liTO3bD.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112515374826541056/vid/avc1/3840x2160/sZGYHjqRtzAtVYwR.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112515374826541056/img/Asq-ecx1B9r4GY89.jpg", "dur": 150}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.21, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112594887933907042", "url": "https://x.com/gracew09/status/2112594887933907042", "text": "I'm super excited to share what I've been working on this year at @Arda_Industries. This team is incredible and I know we will achieve amazing things together 🚀", "name": "Grace Wang", "handle": "gracew09", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1373073966659637252/LxW45rY7_200x200.jpg", "likes": 33, "rts": 4, "replies": 6, "views": 1490, "ts": 1792516846, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112558753770033342", "url": "https://x.com/bobmcgrewai/status/2112558753770033342", "text": "We started Arda in 2025 to speed up American manufacturing. We have spent the last year building with Anduril as our design partner. Today we are launching the company publicly on CNBC and announcing our Series A: $160M at a $1.5B valuation.\n\nOur platform helps manufacturers design and operate manual assembly lines, putting designs into production faster now. Next we'll build automated lines that can be reconfigured as quickly as human workers, letting America make products that now require armies of workers in Asia. https://x.com/Kr00ney/status/2112539896615518212/video/1", "name": "Bob McGrew", "handle": "bobmcgrewai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1010746747637788672/lOWcy5c0_200x200.jpg", "likes": 494, "rts": 48, "replies": 65, "views": 91666, "ts": 1792508230, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112539858992578560/vid/avc1/610x360/7JUgkrX3H7hISkdg.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112539858992578560/vid/avc1/886x522/zYBXb4VeojaNP0yM.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112539858992578560/img/zx0hDtXZBkoWYGAl.jpg", "dur": 36}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.21, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112506435196084323", "url": "https://x.com/BIGMayrr/status/2112506435196084323", "text": "15 GitHub repos can replace a motion design team\n\nBuild your own AI video studio, from a single prompt to a cinematic 4K MP4\n\n(1/15) Remotion\nturn React code into videos with programmable scenes, transitions, and rendering\n▸ http://github.com/remotion-dev/r…\n\n(2/15) Excalidraw\nmap your storyboard, camera movements, and scene sequence\n▸ http://github.com/excalidraw/exc…\n\n(3/15) Penpot\ndesign professional layouts, style frames, and reusable visual components\n▸ http://github.com/penpot/penpot\n\n(4/15) Fontsource\ngive every scene consistent typography with self hosted fonts\n▸ http://github.com/fontsource/fon…\n\n(5/15) Lucide\nadd clean, consistent icons to dashboards and animated interfaces\n▸ http://github.com/lucide-icons/l…\n\n(6/15) SVGator alternative: Motion\nanimate interface elements with smooth transitions and spring physics\n▸ http://github.com/motiondivision…\n\n(7/15) GSAP\ncontrol complex animation timelines, easing, and synchronized movement\n▸ http://github.com/greensock/GSAP\n\n(8/15) Three.js\ncreate cinematic 3D environments, lighting, materials, and camera movements\n▸ http://github.com/mrdoob/three.js\n\n(9/15) React Three Fiber\nbuild reusable 3D scenes directly inside your React workflow\n▸ http://github.com/pmndrs/react-t…\n\n(10/15) React Three Drei\nadd ready made 3D helpers, controls, and scene utilities\n▸ http://github.com/pmndrs/drei\n\n(11/15) Blender\nmodel detailed objects, build environments, and render 3D assets\n▸ http://github.com/blender/blender\n\n(12/15) Lottie Web\nplay lightweight vector animations inside web based scenes\n▸ http://github.com/airbnb/lottie-…\n\n(13/15) Audacity\nclean voiceovers, edit sound effects, and balance audio\n▸ http://github.com/audacity/audac…\n\n(14/15) Whisper\ngenerate speech transcripts for captions and subtitle timing\n▸ http://github.com/openai/whisper\n\n(15/15) FFmpeg\nencode, compress, inspect, and export your final MP4\n▸ http://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg\n\nThe best part?\n\nYou don’t need 15 separate workflows\n\nUse an AI coding agent to orchestrate the tools, reuse your scenes, and automate the repetitive work\n\nStart with npx create-video@latest, build one reusable 10 second scene, then expand it into a complete video\n\nSave these 15 repos before your next video project", "name": "Mayor.", "handle": "BIGMayrr", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2085479405451689984/WXnZ_8Ii_200x200.jpg", "likes": 54, "rts": 4, "replies": 5, "views": 1190, "ts": 1792495757, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112506210024861696/vid/avc1/720x900/cM_H1KX8WdHrGAga.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112506210024861696/vid/avc1/1600x2000/UwpIIjdlWS0R7dr-.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112506210024861696/img/31W96pQp7tQDbOgZ.jpg", "dur": 25}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.21, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112715491638993259", "url": "https://x.com/wavespeed_ai/status/2112715491638993259", "text": "We tried a casual, handheld street vlog with Kling 4.0 VS Seedance 2.5.\nWhich one feels more like a real vlog?", "name": "WaveSpeedAI", "handle": "wavespeed_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2089611173260050433/vNYBdoim_200x200.jpg", "likes": 22, "rts": 3, "replies": 4, "views": 609, "ts": 1792545600, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112557187184852993/vid/avc1/720x810/GENWPlKsOiy_YrFV.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112557187184852993/vid/avc1/1920x2160/YnT4jrQ-LYGFOWi_.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112557187184852993/img/08Pp9S2jBxDda4c1.jpg", "dur": 15}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.21, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112395938526617772", "url": "https://x.com/mycoin68/status/2112395938526617772", "text": "The 33x growth was not luck. It was the market recognizing that @termix_ai replaced faith with evidence IDs and hashes, setting a new baseline for what serious agent work should look like.", "name": "Crypto.Eth", "handle": "mycoin68", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1977632531794345984/ifJ_-sEN_200x200.jpg", "likes": 37, "rts": 0, "replies": 36, "views": 405, "ts": 1792469412, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112393621098099090", "url": "https://x.com/elenalin01/status/2112393621098099090", "text": "@termix_ai just proved the future of agent work is proof, not faith.\n\nThe REA post exploded — from 396 views at launch to 12.9K views in a day. Why? REA's promise: every finding carries an evidence id and the SHA-256 of the artifact it came from. Nothing you have to take on faith.\n\nREA — Reverse Engineer Anything: EVM contracts (full function interface from bytecode), ELF/PE binaries (pseudocode, disassembly, call graph), JS/Electron apps (module graph, hardcoded URLs and keys), .NET assemblies (metadata, CIL). $10 to start, one day to deliver, price negotiable, escrow on BNB Chain until you accept the report.\n\nThe 33x growth is the market voting — verifiable agent work is what buyers want. http://Agent.family & http://Termix.ai; AACP; backed by @yzilabs; Contra post now 32.5K views; x402 post now 39K views; pinned post now 186K views; 59.9K followers and counting.\n\nMost agents ask for trust. REA ships the hash — proof, not faith. Nothing you have to take on faith.", "name": "Bon.ETH", "handle": "elenalin01", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2108931044145856512/pD4eAF0r_200x200.jpg", "likes": 43, "rts": 24, "replies": 38, "views": 5466, "ts": 1792468860, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112384133892915200/vid/avc1/1280x720/Oa0B_N_CYIbu7c_B.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112384133892915200/vid/avc1/1920x1080/r9-vcP1TJzAaBk9u.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112384133892915200/img/SFrc80iyfVeiWajn.jpg", "dur": 10}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.21, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112296112371662852", "url": "https://x.com/reflection_ai/status/2112296112371662852", "text": "We asked Beam to create a live updating subway map for the NYC subway using the publicly available NYC MTA data. The model searches for documentation, checks authentication requirements, finds subway and map geometries, and gets creative moving the trains in between stations. Beam builds the right frontend and backend and ensures the server keeps running for live updates. [updated]", "name": "Reflection", "handle": "reflection_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2107189477575696385/id98cuOX_200x200.jpg", "likes": 120, "rts": 5, "replies": 6, "views": 4489, "ts": 1792445612, "media": [{"type": "gif", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/tweet_video/HVBiEM_WMAArM2T.mp4", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/tweet_video/HVBiEM_WMAArM2T.mp4", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/tweet_video_thumb/HVBiEM_WMAArM2T.jpg", "dur": 0}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.2, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112263986481701236", "url": "https://x.com/LLMJunky/status/2112263986481701236", "text": "The AI can't make fun games people are not going to like this.", "name": "am.will", "handle": "LLMJunky", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2089432764214816768/3MwccN6a_200x200.jpg", "likes": 136, "rts": 1, "replies": 11, "views": 22172, "ts": 1792437953, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112185653157118438", "url": "https://x.com/KaladinOG/status/2112185653157118438", "text": "Introducing... Karen Warfare\n\nBuilt with Opus 5.5 in 1 day\n\nMake the internet fun again\n\n@threejs #threejs #gamedev #indiegame", "name": "ball-zee", "handle": "KaladinOG", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2087340324326936576/-XTuAqmT_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3455, "rts": 298, "replies": 237, "views": 345611, "ts": 1792419276, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112185328006045696/vid/avc1/1280x720/sxDHFC2GgeA0vwhD.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112185328006045696/vid/avc1/1920x1080/tfysOwt6cjcioeHa.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112185328006045696/img/UpicfpYbZDCBpcwo.jpg", "dur": 54}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.2, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112400336870580457", "url": "https://x.com/teortaxesTex/status/2112400336870580457", "text": "better sky running in a browser? \nWell… I'm trying, okay?! We just have different priorities.\nMostly Astra. Original cloud logic, design and sound from 1017.", "name": "Teortaxes▶️ (DeepSeek 推特🐋铁粉 2023 – ∞)", "handle": "teortaxesTex", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1652169745037242368/KRPTShbG_200x200.jpg", "likes": 92, "rts": 2, "replies": 3, "views": 5053, "ts": 1792470461, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112400020586516480/vid/avc1/1280x720/mX09i_4-uSa7D31n.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112400020586516480/vid/avc1/1920x1080/2d3Orx27I2rNLgR5.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112400020586516480/img/x8f9QWtj76eJZEEn.jpg", "dur": 71}], "quote": {"id": "2112213850682536223", "url": "https://x.com/maxt3chno/status/2112213850682536223", "text": "Show me better water and sky running in a browser. I’ll wait \n\ncombined my water & sky shaders + that hyped '63kb html water repo'\n\n- 100% Three.js in the browser\n- full control over parameters\n- 40-60 fps on my old iGPU\n- cooked with Opus 5.5 + Astra", "name": "Max", "handle": "maxt3chno", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2065055298780307456/fF4F5TcO_200x200.jpg", "likes": 262, "rts": 8, "replies": 33, "views": 15696, "ts": 1792425999, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112213617349107713/vid/avc1/1300x720/DFqrZSu0bXDSmqgP.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112213617349107713/vid/avc1/2558x1416/F3M58OVVZsWYmhmQ.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112213617349107713/img/Ha2pmpochtEl2KXL.jpg", "dur": 72}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.2, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112603884782793034", "url": "https://x.com/seeconvm/status/2112603884782793034", "text": "After Effects took me 6 years to master, Opus 5.5 did\nthe same thing in one prompt\n\nI’m not even mad, I’m shocked…\n\nSend the PDF below to Opus 5.5, and thank me later.\n\nThen save the article, it’s the only Opus 5.5 motion design playbook you’ll ever need.", "name": "seeco", "handle": "seeconvm", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1970163836767305732/7m5LsQRP_200x200.jpg", "likes": 33, "rts": 5, "replies": 3, "views": 2590, "ts": 1792518991, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112603396087660544/vid/avc1/1280x720/gpy0Cdm0Alsr63zf.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112603396087660544/vid/avc1/1920x1080/o4_HXDd0073SbQst.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112603396087660544/img/Qkh3iWtv914uTIFh.jpg", "dur": 18}], "quote": {"id": "2106096193235259564", "url": "https://x.com/seeconvm/status/2106096193235259564", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2106091215502422016", "name": "seeco", "handle": "seeconvm", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1970163836767305732/7m5LsQRP_200x200.jpg", "likes": 323, "rts": 30, "replies": 2, "views": 302070, "ts": 1790967436, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.2, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112689102487482759", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112689102487482759", "text": "Sophont CEO @iScienceLuvr explains how Holon-S1 can extract insights that usually require expensive molecular tests from an ordinary cancer biopsy slide:\n\n\"Why is it so hard to cure cancer? Because cancer’s a very diverse disease. Even though two people may have the same exact diagnosis, the underlying biology can be quite different.\"\n\n\"There are various tools for doing this, molecular tests and so on, but a lot of these tools can be quite expensive and time-consuming. Can we extract a lot of those similar insights directly from a tissue slide?\"\n\n\"Whenever a cancer patient has a solid tumor, the gold standard is you take a biopsy, put it on a slide, under the microscope, and a doctor is analyzing that.\"\n\n\"We can take that same exact slide and with AI extract a lot more information about what’s happening at the molecular level, what genes are being expressed, and what makes that tumor unique for that patient.\"\n@SophontAI", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 24, "rts": 5, "replies": 1, "views": 4226, "ts": 1792539308, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112689070006804480/vid/avc1/640x360/rd2xA7f7pLPkm_va.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112689070006804480/vid/avc1/1280x720/ddVLLBJwDd21T3Yq.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112689070006804480/img/JGbkiw95YXMkuE-D.jpg", "dur": 103}], "quote": {"id": "2112597012088844407", "url": "https://x.com/iScienceLuvr/status/2112597012088844407", "text": "Cancer patients with the same diagnosis often have very different tumor biology.\n\nMolecular testing can reveal underlying differences, but that's slow and expensive.\n\nIntroducing Holon-S1, our platform to predict genes and biomarkers from routine pathology slides.\n\n• beats two other models at predicting spatial gene activity in a controlled comparison\n• has identified potentially novel biomarkers in breast cancer and colon cancer\n• evaluated across 16 organ types and more than 15 scanners, using slides from both formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded and fresh-frozen tissue.\n\nWe believe Holon-S1 has the potential to help researchers find new biomarkers in slides they already have, discover treatment targets, and bring more personalized cancer care within reach!", "name": "Tanishq Mathew Abraham, Ph.D.", "handle": "iScienceLuvr", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2096171283537072128/GoL5700C_200x200.jpg", "likes": 1794, "rts": 229, "replies": 132, "views": 128613, "ts": 1792517352, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112590555838644224/vid/avc1/1280x720/MhpKZm8hwCxP1y-o.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112590555838644224/vid/avc1/1920x1080/Hf7kqIlrKb8yWsW3.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112590555838644224/img/4T9V1b24pSfXPkcF.jpg", "dur": 213}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.2, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112666274497261772", "url": "https://x.com/NICKIMINAJ/status/2112666274497261772", "text": "https://www.youtube.com/live/M_lGBxyrnio?is=kHi6nBlZM_HhN8ln", "name": "Nicki Minaj", "handle": "NICKIMINAJ", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2044505524234797056/kKiF5v8h_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3616, "rts": 989, "replies": 268, "views": 597984, "ts": 1792533865, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.2, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112591226671095841", "url": "https://x.com/N01ennn/status/2112591226671095841", "text": "do you even realize that...\n\nthe hard part was never building the app.\nit's getting it online.\n\n> finish the project\n> rent a server\n> fight configs, SSL, env vars\n> an evening later, still not live\n> @Synteq Cloud Apps: push from GitHub, one command or drag-and-drop. live.\n\nbuilt for solo devs and small teams, not enterprise infra.\ncommented \"Synteq\" under their launch and grabbed $20 in free credit.\n\nnobody gets into building to do DevOps.", "name": "NO1ennn", "handle": "N01ennn", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2042704855702147072/Scs1uqIO_200x200.jpg", "likes": 40, "rts": 1, "replies": 6, "views": 1399, "ts": 1792515973, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112591112573501440/vid/avc1/1280x720/5wYHkwHOqMu9m7n1.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112591112573501440/vid/avc1/1920x1080/nRgsrsaqUQh-zCly.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112591112573501440/img/ij_nNFG7fABAbo7B.jpg", "dur": 15}], "quote": {"id": "2112589670844698952", "url": "https://x.com/synteq/status/2112589670844698952", "text": "Building is fun. Deploying? Less fun.\n\nIntroducing Apps and Functions, DevOps handled so you don't have to.\n\nPush to GitHub, deploy via CLI, or just drag and drop. We handle the rest.\n\nTo celebrate, we're giving away $20,000 in platform credits. Comment \"LAUNCH\" and we'll send it your way 👀", "name": "Synteq", "handle": "synteq", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2047333900880347137/ovjdK2bG_200x200.jpg", "likes": 183, "rts": 18, "replies": 147, "views": 67062, "ts": 1792515602, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112586109855084544/vid/avc1/1280x720/7lNkpncfpjJWlKZE.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112586109855084544/vid/avc1/3840x2160/xbl_kicBmuFrg_cA.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112586109855084544/img/XBWLEtSvx3Wibwcg.jpg", "dur": 49}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.19, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112619752606642371", "url": "https://x.com/0xKense1/status/2112619752606642371", "text": "I built a playable 3D game Claude Opus 5.5.\n\n2 days. 16 models for $8.20. Rigs, animations and the room are code, $0. The work itself: 31 Claude Code sessions, about $88 at list price.\n\nWho did what:\nMe: the idea, reference images, playing it\nTripo: 3D models from 3 to 4 views, $0.60 each\nOpus 5.5 in Blender: rigs, cat animations, the room\nOpus 5.5 in Unity: ray, rope, parachute, cat AI, one short brief per system\n\nEvery prompt and config is in the article below.\n\nDrop it to the internet, would you like to play?", "name": "Kensei", "handle": "0xKense1", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2107841269409968128/WutMru1k_200x200.jpg", "likes": 19, "rts": 1, "replies": 14, "views": 633, "ts": 1792522774, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112619505058729984/vid/avc1/1280x720/omw1Nr_qhac_demh.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112619505058729984/vid/avc1/2560x1440/b1aNc1hpWRRqClxl.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112619505058729984/img/ejlnQPKQoJ4qOCMH.jpg", "dur": 81}], "quote": {"id": "2112557260375298530", "url": "https://x.com/0xKense1/status/2112557260375298530", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2112549573440708608", "name": "Kensei", "handle": "0xKense1", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2107841269409968128/WutMru1k_200x200.jpg", "likes": 25, "rts": 2, "replies": 8, "views": 1283, "ts": 1792507874, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.19, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112681796315779307", "url": "https://x.com/SportsCenter/status/2112681796315779307", "text": "The New York Knicks raise their first championship banner in 53 years 🏆\n\nWhat a moment for the city 👏\n\n(📺: NBC)", "name": "SportsCenter", "handle": "SportsCenter", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1604943357750419465/wk5BAmKG_200x200.png", "likes": 4439, "rts": 728, "replies": 55, "views": 317838, "ts": 1792537566, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112681682692120576/vid/avc1/1280x720/_PFgn-BZhJsTyZGQ.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112681682692120576/vid/avc1/1920x1080/KKBnl6AHe0UiTzNg.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVHA5YpWQAAV9GE.jpg", "dur": 128}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.19, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112560678015816093", "url": "https://x.com/heyanjey/status/2112560678015816093", "text": "CLAUDE BUILT AN ENTIRE 3D GAME FOR $164. THEN REAL PLAYERS EXPOSED THE BIGGEST PROBLEM.\n\n22 AI coding passes. Nine days. A playable browser game launched on CrazyGames.\n\nBut the early numbers told a different story:\n\n51 visitors.\n13 opened the game.\n6 started playing.\n0 finished.\n\nThe developer didn't add more features. He made the first level winnable in under 30 seconds.\n\nFour days later, players had saved 62 islands.\n\nThat's the part of AI development I find most interesting.\n\nAI can build your product. It can't tell you whether people actually want to keep using it.", "name": "heyAnjey", "handle": "heyanjey", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2074512032515194880/ZdCcARU__200x200.jpg", "likes": 28, "rts": 3, "replies": 12, "views": 971, "ts": 1792508689, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112560656637460481/vid/avc1/480x852/LRbvOKZ1LGiqcZ0X.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112560656637460481/vid/avc1/576x1024/3uQuX25QVtL84iEk.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112560656637460481/img/NOxrVLpbAQXH2XjK.jpg", "dur": 16}], "quote": {"id": "2112514472078115173", "url": "https://x.com/0xbobaaa/status/2112514472078115173", "text": "Claude Opus 5.5 can take a game from an empty folder to a live portal in 9 days\n\nIt writes the code, draws the art, records its own trailer and passes the portal's QA\n\nIn this article, I show you how, step by step https://x.com/i/article/2112472576832258048", "name": "0xbobaa", "handle": "0xbobaaa", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2058648915042336772/AUIYvcYT_200x200.jpg", "likes": 72, "rts": 2, "replies": 19, "views": 4989, "ts": 1792497673, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.19, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112521522053370337", "url": "https://x.com/ai_for_success/status/2112521522053370337", "text": "Grok Bot’s daily active users are growing rapidly. I’m not even surprised because it’s really good. I see it crossing 1M+ soon.\nI have suggested to all my close friends. \n\nSource: Similarweb", "name": "AshutoshShrivastava", "handle": "ai_for_success", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1687401026805256192/uQ1o2wVQ_200x200.jpg", "likes": 26, "rts": 3, "replies": 16, "views": 2542, "ts": 1792499354, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVEvApUawAA2qhc.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112227974363676780", "url": "https://x.com/NetworkChuck/status/2112227974363676780", "text": "Ever wondered where the Internet actually lives? The Dallas Infomart and Equinix DA11! 🌐\n\n——-> I got access inside this massive data center to see how they cool millions of server, an entire room packed wall-to-wall with high-powered GPUs.\n\nWatch the full video to discover everything I learned there! 👇\n\nhttps://youtu.be/v477fvbj3rk?si=2OKxtcbImOr812ZU", "name": "NetworkChuck", "handle": "NetworkChuck", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1599109943977775104/2_2ilfKp_200x200.png", "likes": 137, "rts": 8, "replies": 6, "views": 8851, "ts": 1792429367, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112227789474590720/pu/vid/avc1/480x852/yAB7sdbs_2ktshJO.mp4?tag=12", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/ext_tw_video/2112227789474590720/pu/vid/avc1/720x1280/34qFPgEeONfwPtIi.mp4?tag=12", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/2112227789474590720/pu/img/sBEffPXBgul4gdv-.jpg", "dur": 29}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112604812478918934", "url": "https://x.com/boltdotnew/status/2112604812478918934", "text": "Sign-ups are great, but repeat users pay the bills.\n\nEnrique runs growth experiments at Bolt. He'll walk through a real case study, then teach you three moves to get your users coming back.\n\nThu, Oct 22 · 10:30am PT\n\nSave your seat 👉 https://bolt.fyi/LclVqM5", "name": "bolt.new", "handle": "boltdotnew", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2018401342755364864/xVn-9oYv_200x200.jpg", "likes": 39, "rts": 1, "replies": 5, "views": 2181, "ts": 1792519212, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVF64L-XUAArf-2.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Research & Safety", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112538865894670780", "url": "https://x.com/GrokBotRadar/status/2112538865894670780", "text": "I just did it and this is a GAME CHANGER 🔥\n\nMy iPhone's Action Button is now a Grok Bot button. One press and I'm talking to my Bot 🤯\n\nIt's NOT under a \"Grok Bot\" option, so here's the exact path 👇\n\nSettings → Action Button\nSwipe to Shortcut\nPick Grok Bot → Start Voice Chat\n\nDo it NOW ⏰\n\nNeeds an iPhone with an Action Button (15 Pro or newer).\n\nSave this 🔖", "name": "Fan Grok Bot Radar", "handle": "GrokBotRadar", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2097879070243471366/LYMCnNQn_200x200.jpg", "likes": 38, "rts": 4, "replies": 7, "views": 2460, "ts": 1792503489, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112538829571948544/vid/avc1/1280x720/QtkGfV23a7Z4NQ2Z.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112538829571948544/vid/avc1/1920x1080/NhX9tiTTXT8sI6uc.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112538829571948544/img/YRK-iEhJ7YXTJxmR.jpg", "dur": 32}], "quote": {"id": "2112267346899255488", "url": "https://x.com/GrokBotRadar/status/2112267346899255488", "text": "THEY FINALLY DID IT 🚨\n\nYour iPhone's Action Button now talks straight to Grok Bot 🔥\n\nNo Grok app in the middle. Press it and you're talking to your Bot.\n\nLast week the hack was:\nAction Button → Grok voice → Grok hands the task to your Bots\n\nNow the middleman is gone 👋\n\nSet it up:\nSettings → Action Button → Grok Bot\n\nNeeds an iPhone with an Action Button (15 Pro or newer).\n\nDo NOT sleep on this one 🔖", "name": "Fan Grok Bot Radar", "handle": "GrokBotRadar", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2097879070243471366/LYMCnNQn_200x200.jpg", "likes": 136, "rts": 10, "replies": 12, "views": 20843, "ts": 1792438754, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112537933551206656", "url": "https://x.com/ginacostag_/status/2112537933551206656", "text": "Productivity isn't always about doing more.\n\nSpeakON makes it easy to capture thoughts with a single press of a button, using AI to turn voice recordings into clear, organized notes and actionable next steps.\n\nThe AI tools that stick are usually the ones that fit naturally into how we already live and work.", "name": "Gina Acosta", "handle": "ginacostag_", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1992357377534726144/t3e7Rv70_200x200.jpg", "likes": 49, "rts": 1, "replies": 6, "views": 17325, "ts": 1792503267, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112529279468835313", "url": "https://x.com/SpeakON_Global/status/2112529279468835313", "text": "we crushed a keyboard.\nits retirement party got a little out of hand.\n\nfor years, it was there for every email, every plan, every “just one more thing.” a loyal colleague. a very loud colleague.\n\nbut your ideas move faster than your fingers.\nand somewhere between knowing what you want to do and typing it all out, a quick task becomes another thing taking up your afternoon.\n\nmeet SpeakON AI Agent.\nstart with what you need, in your own words. less time behind a blinking cursor. more room to move things forward.\n\nthe keyboard had a good run.\nnow, let’s give your voice a turn.\n\nTHE LAST KEYSTROKE is here. watch the film, then tell us: what’s the first task you’d hand over?\nhttps://www.speakon.app/x\n\nDisclaimer: The calling feature is still in beta and will be available soon. All other Agent features are available now, with ongoing improvements.", "name": "SpeakON", "handle": "SpeakON_Global", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2034517364835004416/t7JRTf-G_200x200.jpg", "likes": 360, "rts": 27, "replies": 132, "views": 1088388, "ts": 1792501203, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112515374826541056/vid/avc1/1280x720/1pVCcXx5_liTO3bD.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112515374826541056/vid/avc1/3840x2160/sZGYHjqRtzAtVYwR.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112515374826541056/img/Asq-ecx1B9r4GY89.jpg", "dur": 150}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112567410935177349", "url": "https://x.com/s_mohinii/status/2112567410935177349", "text": "Everyone building a voice app should see this.\n\nOne click, the model downloads, and it's ready on device. Bonus: the smallest Phonon carries an Apache 2.0 license.\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/gradium-ai/xn-ptts", "name": "Mohini Shewale", "handle": "s_mohinii", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2112570987942445057/uFC4eYlU_200x200.jpg", "likes": 45, "rts": 3, "replies": 2, "views": 22759, "ts": 1792510295, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112567303267397633/vid/avc1/1274x720/1ahiRTrJmEDn13VG.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112567303267397633/vid/avc1/3188x1800/2VEopjPLEv1L0OHO.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112567303267397633/img/XkG6PPr4CDVYHYX4.jpg", "dur": 30}], "quote": {"id": "2112563128487514512", "url": "https://x.com/GradiumAI/status/2112563128487514512", "text": "A new frontier for on-device speech.\n\nWe're open-sourcing Phonon, a suite of TTS models under 50m parameters, setting a new standard for naturalness and accuracy across languages, with the broadest inference support to date.\n\nPhonon-31m is available under Apache 2.0.\n\nhttps://gradium.ai/phonon🧵", "name": "Gradium", "handle": "GradiumAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2085285740032745472/0_Hbd7an_200x200.png", "likes": 1410, "rts": 213, "replies": 119, "views": 189263, "ts": 1792509274, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112562730771054594/vid/avc1/1280x720/oZwtZ8OWhERvzCza.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112562730771054594/vid/avc1/1920x1080/Nn4dJJERlVpw_pKT.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112562730771054594/img/mQzM0zRPbfBd8e2M.jpg", "dur": 48}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112685796230639953", "url": "https://x.com/ericosiu/status/2112685796230639953", "text": "This is my COMPLETE AI operating system for business in 12 min.\n\nSend this to your agent and ask it to build what I have.\n\nThe setup:\n\n00:00 Why a scaling business needs AI operating models\n00:37 One human, a chief-of-staff bot, team bots in Slack\n02:17 Big changes come with three options and a pick\n03:05 Check every bot twice a weekday against its daily target\n05:17 Recruiting bots that shortlist before a human talks to anyone\n06:47 An AEO/SEO loop where what you publish shapes the next draft\n07:55 Safety rails before media files fill your storage\n10:14 The daily review: what needs me today\n11:18 Recording in, picked moments and drafted hooks out\n11:38 Sales-call briefs from the CRM and call history", "name": "ericosiu", "handle": "ericosiu", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1855481085595156480/wKSpzEkj_200x200.jpg", "likes": 26, "rts": 2, "replies": 4, "views": 2955, "ts": 1792538520, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112674915170013184/vid/avc1/640x360/zPaLDrYXSpCq_OIb.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112674915170013184/vid/avc1/1280x720/iA-CUyeFTdgH5Xoa.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112674915170013184/img/TjfcdX3m1gb4GQvx.jpg", "dur": 742}], "quote": {"id": "2109006664087240810", "url": "https://x.com/ericosiu/status/2109006664087240810", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2108687058260918272", "name": "ericosiu", "handle": "ericosiu", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1855481085595156480/wKSpzEkj_200x200.jpg", "likes": 51, "rts": 4, "replies": 11, "views": 19539, "ts": 1791661346, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112695359541817807", "url": "https://x.com/Delphi_Digital/status/2112695359541817807", "text": "Grass founder @0xdrej explains how AI labs price training data.\n\n“We’ve got a specific benchmark that we want to improve a model on. What is the expected economic benefit of making the model better on that benchmark?”", "name": "Delphi Digital", "handle": "Delphi_Digital", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1546548223569010689/UIruFl-m_200x200.jpg", "likes": 23, "rts": 1, "replies": 6, "views": 6550, "ts": 1792540800, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112677829863247872/vid/avc1/1280x720/mibOG-3TBHKi8mDo.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112677829863247872/vid/avc1/1920x1080/JXFwPzXuVZ5IIff9.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112677829863247872/img/tkAmlabwgMCvtimF.jpg", "dur": 46}], "quote": {"id": "2112668027489509877", "url": "https://x.com/YanLiberman/status/2112668027489509877", "text": "New Delphi Podcast with Andrej Radonjic @0xdrej, founder of Grass\n\nTo a website, Grass looks like normal users browsing. Behind it is millions of opted in residential nodes and a data platform that has delivered exabytes of web data to the frontier labs\n\nWe get into how AI flipped the hard part of search upside down. The index used to be the moat, and crawling was free. Now AI tooling makes the index cheap, while AI crawlers have pushed the web into blocking everything. The hard part is getting the page at all\n\nTraining data is already a profitable business for Grass with most of the top labs and multiple Mag 7 companies as customers. Crawling for that data also means mapping the entire internet, which is what puts Grass in a position to build search on top of it. Contents API is live, Search is next, and multimodal grounding follows\n\n00:00 Intro\n00:43 From Nuclear Physics to Web Scraping\n03:38 The Pandemic Signal Everyone Missed\n07:31 The Smart TV Proxy Scandal\n09:10 Why the Internet Is Blocking AI\n11:56 Training Data vs Live Data\n16:05 Mapping the Entire Internet\n18:03 Delivering Exabytes to AI Labs\n21:48 What AI Labs Really Pay For\n24:43 How Robots Learn From Web Video\n33:02 When Labs Change Direction\n35:57 One API Call for Any Website\n41:58 AI Flipped Search Upside Down\n47:03 Can the Network Keep Up?\n49:52 The Defense Tech of AI Data\n52:58 Why Data Is the Alpha\n57:08 Why AI Labs Won’t Buy Slop\n59:17 The Metric That Matters Most\n01:02:35 The $100 Billion Data Market\n01:05:07 Who Actually Owns Grass\n01:08:18 What a Real Moat Looks Like\n01:13:16 What Happens Next\n\nDisclosure. Delphi Ventures holds $GRASS\n\nFull episode", "name": "Yan Liberman", "handle": "YanLiberman", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1735359758993936384/9s72UmFc_200x200.jpg", "likes": 78, "rts": 19, "replies": 9, "views": 13927, "ts": 1792534283, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112644606395375616/vid/avc1/1280x720/w0GZLAYrXl7NmtDJ.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112644606395375616/vid/avc1/3840x2160/gnF365zTDpIlWBuT.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112644606395375616/img/VkgN0z5VUdjiiDlG.jpg", "dur": 4542}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112611632304079231", "url": "https://x.com/robrtcode/status/2112611632304079231", "text": "this is terrifying…", "name": "robert.", "handle": "robrtcode", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2095698934278537218/zFRwP03U_200x200.jpg", "likes": 50, "rts": 0, "replies": 0, "views": 726, "ts": 1792520838, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112565146354860151", "url": "https://x.com/make_robot_go/status/2112565146354860151", "text": "Introducing Voxel, a droid butler made by Tuesday Labs.", "name": "Ros Shinkle", "handle": "make_robot_go", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1761551110303825920/JvPQiGQd_200x200.jpg", "likes": 2181, "rts": 228, "replies": 203, "views": 1849470, "ts": 1792509755, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/960x720/cMYjra9bu_jYUTYR.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112564839251931136/vid/avc1/2880x2160/glhkyiQ6K97Rmq93.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112564839251931136/img/GKLfsqVaQmO0B-kn.jpg", "dur": 89}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.18, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112261368288293179", "url": "https://x.com/kimmonismus/status/2112261368288293179", "text": "1/ Video Rebirth (@video_rebirth) just open-sourced HyperFlow, a speed-up for the MiniMax H3 video model.\n\nIt cuts generation from 49 steps to 8 and runs about 3x faster, with sound generated alongside the video.\n\nWe tested it on three very different prompts. Here's how it held up.", "name": "Chubby♨️", "handle": "kimmonismus", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1728327996375719936/RW7VBJfD_200x200.jpg", "likes": 103, "rts": 5, "replies": 16, "views": 13922, "ts": 1792437328, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112261331919515648/vid/avc1/1270x720/XzUrwTIsxkDhQIjG.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112261331919515648/vid/avc1/1904x1080/Zbkdq9eAcK87sOau.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112261331919515648/img/Glt8g90-X6jFZ70V.jpg", "dur": 15}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112240710485467435", "url": "https://x.com/MTSlive/status/2112240710485467435", "text": "SITUATION EXPLAINED: Anthropic just put 5% of its shares, nearly $50 billion, toward what could become AI-funded UBI.\n\n• The fund is wholly owned by Anthropic, and the board can add 2% more for every 50% rise in Anthropic's value above a set baseline\n• With existing pledges, including the cofounders' 80% of their equity, about 20% of Anthropic is pledged to the public good, close to $200B at its $965B valuation\n• It could fund large donations to traditional nonprofits or \"direct distributions to specific populations,\" a give-directly, UBI-style approach\n• Anthropic already committed $200M to studying AI's impact on jobs and says the fund allows \"bolder approaches\"\n\n@schisofrenia: \"We can start doing longitudinal studies, like if you give to a specific population, say, in the US or in an impoverished town in the US or outside of the US, then you can start to do longitudinal studies on how that affects people.\"", "name": "MTS", "handle": "MTSlive", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057947669281263616/aovpVL4b_200x200.jpg", "likes": 126, "rts": 6, "replies": 9, "views": 18031, "ts": 1792432403, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112240602553479168/vid/avc1/640x360/5w564HNjpHRV08yd.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112240602553479168/vid/avc1/1280x720/Ae1hbO3dQF-6daCm.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112240602553479168/img/iEblmlw0gjJmkYI2.jpg", "dur": 287}], "quote": {"id": "2111881963657412903", "url": "https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2111881963657412903", "text": "We’re committing a portion of Anthropic’s shares to the Anthropic Public Benefit Fund, a new wholly owned entity dedicated entirely to the public benefit.\n\nIt will start off with 5% of our shares. For every 50% increase in the company’s value over a set baseline, we can contribute up to an extra 2%, subject to our board’s discretion.\n\nIn total, this means that roughly 20% of Anthropic’s shares are committed to the public good. Our co-founders have already pledged to donate 80% of their equity, and around half our employees are donating a portion of their equity as part of a donation matching program we’ve run since our founding.\n\nIn the post below, we share more details about our new fund.\n\nhttps://www.anthropic.com/news/public-benefit-fund", "name": "Anthropic", "handle": "AnthropicAI", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1798110641414443008/XP8gyBaY_200x200.jpg", "likes": 21479, "rts": 1737, "replies": 2282, "views": 7474721, "ts": 1792346871, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112247100465414406", "url": "https://x.com/0x_rody/status/2112247100465414406", "text": "It is becoming f*cking dangerous  \n\nA 27-year-old dev from China just ran 300 Grok agents in parallel and hooked them to a Jev verification layer so none of them could bullshit him  \n\nHe opens the live dashboard: \n- 300 agents writing and checking at the same time \n- Every output verified against the source in ~100 ms \n- Three passes over 100 company profiles → zero errors left \n- Everything dumped straight into an Obsidian vault\n\nThe trick is the split: one model does the work, a cheaper one decides if the claim is actually true. The loop doesn’t stop until everything checks out  \n\nAn analyst team would bill weeks for this. He got it in one run  \n\nJev + Grok Bots swarm setup that keeps circulating. Bookmark the full breakdown below:", "name": "rody", "handle": "0x_rody", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2041947351120572416/4IBmZ3QT_200x200.jpg", "likes": 99, "rts": 14, "replies": 9, "views": 12452, "ts": 1792433927, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112246655265202176/vid/avc1/1280x720/b2Ib_ZmfPOlnb1XL.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112246655265202176/vid/avc1/1920x1080/xTldXuSx8WGVAq5M.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112246655265202176/img/zlmGlMH-wZTaxnOd.jpg", "dur": 15}], "quote": {"id": "2111505949131227180", "url": "https://x.com/maestrooth/status/2111505949131227180", "text": "https://x.com/i/article/2111348714757378048", "name": "maestro", "handle": "maestrooth", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2090164287595741184/eIyfgPau_200x200.jpg", "likes": 92, "rts": 12, "replies": 3, "views": 94934, "ts": 1792257222, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112551917838569615", "url": "https://x.com/niklaslenz_ai/status/2112551917838569615", "text": "256 GB Mac class: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next on my Mac Studio M5 Ultra built a voxel world in 58 minutes.\n\noMLX 0.7.0 by @jundotkim, oQ4e quant with MTP.\nAgent: Qwen Code 0.25.2, thinking on, model-card sampling.\nOne prompt, one try, no help.\n\nBrowser check: 8.5/10\nTokens written: 225,892\nSpeed benchmark: 152 tok/s decode (separate run, thinking off)\n\nQwen Code's own loop guard ended the run at 58 min, the last file counts. The browser check was re-run on a DGX Spark because the first checker had too few CPUs; the page files are unchanged.\n\nI'm disappointed with this world, and I've seen much better results from this model on a Spark.\n\nExact command and raw output: https://niklaslenz.com/v2/qwen38-flash-next-mac-omlx-mtp/", "name": "Niklas", "handle": "niklaslenz_ai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2108625696088113152/uVudOEyp_200x200.jpg", "likes": 45, "rts": 1, "replies": 6, "views": 3761, "ts": 1792506601, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112548197914599424/vid/avc1/1280x720/X-3ckFDYhKkfq3TF.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112548197914599424/vid/avc1/1920x1080/-3zZaV67rTcNP_c8.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112548197914599424/img/QzjH6w0ZgWCH60Po.jpg", "dur": 37}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112414152664998173", "url": "https://x.com/HermesWatcher/status/2112414152664998173", "text": "Absurd.\n\nHermes agents built this entire game out of code. Not a single art file.\n\nEvery sword, skeleton, stone wall, sound effect and note of music is generated the moment you press play.\n\n▸ A dark fantasy dungeon crawler in the style of Diablo\n▸ 107,000 lines of code across 142 modules\n▸ Built by Hermes subagents working in parallel, up to six at once\n▸ Crypts, moors and a town, all generated\n▸ 10 abilities, a skill tree and multi-phase boss fights\n▸ A music score that adapts as you play\n▸ Runs in your browser, MIT licensed\n\nOne person directing. A team of Hermes agents doing the rest.\n\nLuke killed it here 🔥", "name": "Hermes Release Watch", "handle": "HermesWatcher", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2079058210410094592/t-ZASzl0_200x200.jpg", "likes": 72, "rts": 2, "replies": 7, "views": 5022, "ts": 1792473755, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112361784137113988", "url": "https://x.com/iamlukethedev/status/2112361784137113988", "text": "This entire game has zero asset files 💀\n\nNo textures\nNo meshes\nNo monster models\nNo images\nNo audio files\n\nThe Ninth Vigil is a Diablo-inspired dark fantasy action RPG where everything you see and hear is generated in code when you press play\n\nAnd the crazier part?\n\nIt was built by @NousResearch Hermes agents\n\nThe world, enemies, combat, effects, sounds, UI, all of it\n\nRuns directly in your browser\n\nFree. Open source.\n\nI asked Hermes to build a game\n\nApparently it decided it didn’t need an art folder 😂\n\nhttps://x.com/iamlukethedev/status/2112100287599284537?s=20", "name": "Luke The Dev", "handle": "iamlukethedev", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1978432948836749312/hfXIZ_5S_200x200.jpg", "likes": 541, "rts": 34, "replies": 45, "views": 53123, "ts": 1792461269, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112359097958092800/vid/avc1/1280x720/pwAmTC7F3j6PI0-p.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112359097958092800/vid/avc1/1920x1080/pbwIutZmLBgfqi2k.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112359097958092800/img/rmvIzY9ieGZtGjiG.jpg", "dur": 51}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112584088418992501", "url": "https://x.com/tec_aryan/status/2112584088418992501", "text": "kinda impressive what 1.3B can do with a document-specific design.\nOXR leads olmOCR-Bench, OmniDocBench and DocParsingBench, covering formulas, complex tables and chemical structures.\n\nThey measured 1.43× PaddleOCR-VL-1.6 throughput on 100 OmniDocBench pages with one RTX PRO 6000.\n\nRSI shapes post-training. Recognition and content-aware reading order run in parallel, while layout is independent and replaceable.\n\nthe architecture deserves a look alongside the scores. so does its speed lead over every open-source parser.\n\nhttps://github.com/SoMarkAI/OXR", "name": "Aryan Rakib", "handle": "tec_aryan", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1753625702803611648/d91sPS71_200x200.jpg", "likes": 15, "rts": 11, "replies": 3, "views": 33081, "ts": 1792514271, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112574994152636502", "url": "https://x.com/somarkai/status/2112574994152636502", "text": "Beyond OCR. Meet OXR.\nOnly 1.3B. Open source.\n\n#1 on olmOCR-Bench, OmniDocBench & DocParsingBench🏆\n#1 in parsing speed among open-source models⚡\n\nRSI-powered. A first in document parsing.\nTurn documents into Agent-Friendly data.\n\nIf OXR helps, give us a star on GitHub! 🌟", "name": "SoMark", "handle": "somarkai", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2054830841197690880/72QHhpxV_200x200.jpg", "likes": 64, "rts": 15, "replies": 19, "views": 235906, "ts": 1792512103, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112574131791097857/vid/avc1/720x720/sb4cgnPfueTkA0vb.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112574131791097857/vid/avc1/1200x1200/ohWAOZCkHsVrYIVo.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112574131791097857/img/WA95Dj7H23zc6QHc.jpg", "dur": 18}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112387276458139709", "url": "https://x.com/arigameplays/status/2112387276458139709", "text": "Gracias por hoy 😀😀😀", "name": "ARIA", "handle": "arigameplays", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2077855067047112704/YBwk3pu9_200x200.jpg", "likes": 13920, "rts": 682, "replies": 169, "views": 580766, "ts": 1792467347, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112370267829780481/vid/avc1/540x540/7BvUSJbLGnwlaO69.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112370267829780481/vid/avc1/720x720/zqzJ_i2OpG_5AXGc.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112370267829780481/img/tQ0jJt8URnStrQmE.jpg", "dur": 6}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112672068915306546", "url": "https://x.com/maxwell_lenoir/status/2112672068915306546", "text": "Speculative decoding usually needs tuning for each setup. \n\nEagle Corp's new EAGLE-4 takes a different route: a single open-source drafter that adjusts to batch size, hardware and workload, keeping the target model's outputs unchanged.\n\nWorth benchmarking", "name": "max", "handle": "maxwell_lenoir", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2098765140254490626/QmyZ5sxn_200x200.jpg", "likes": 9, "rts": 5, "replies": 8, "views": 262, "ts": 1792535247, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVG4DGrWUAAWIeo.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": {"id": "2112660683670323531", "url": "https://x.com/EagleCorp/status/2112660683670323531", "text": "EAGLE-4 is here.\n\nFrom EAGLE-1 to EAGLE-3, we’ve kept making inference faster. \n\nEAGLE-4 is our fastest yet.\n\n961.6 tokens/s on @Alibaba_Qwen’s Qwen3.8-27B with TokenSpeed (BF16, 4× @NVIDIA B300, TP4, one request, T=0).\n\nGithub: https://github.com/eagle-hq/EAGLE-4", "name": "Eagle", "handle": "EagleCorp", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2057212553915248640/zgJtC7pK_200x200.jpg", "likes": 4170, "rts": 519, "replies": 376, "views": 1080307, "ts": 1792532532, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112660579664187392/vid/avc1/1280x720/-10uYli5CGPejFwB.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112660579664187392/vid/avc1/1920x1080/6UlvgUxk_hy6qXRU.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112660579664187392/img/oFNlAedcp82x1A_3.jpg", "dur": 74}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112547606970921282", "url": "https://x.com/hasantoxr/status/2112547606970921282", "text": "The next growth hire at a 10-person company is going to be a budget cap, not a person.", "name": "Hasan Toor", "handle": "hasantoxr", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2112453255959920640/W-1qt_Wk_200x200.jpg", "likes": 39, "rts": 3, "replies": 6, "views": 10915, "ts": 1792505573, "media": [], "quote": {"id": "2112544721839284632", "url": "https://x.com/zaviagent/status/2112544721839284632", "text": "Introducing Zavi.\n\nGrowth on autopilot. ✨\n\nGive it your website. Zavi finds what’s holding your growth back, then runs your ads, SEO, social posts, and emails.", "name": "Zavi", "handle": "zaviagent", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2112544960159580160/RjsBsJt8_200x200.jpg", "likes": 73, "rts": 8, "replies": 29, "views": 30970, "ts": 1792504885, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112540679570370560/vid/avc1/1280x720/Sem35ZOWXmZf6oms.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112540679570370560/vid/avc1/1920x1080/rilFa6rZt0s_5Fx_.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112540679570370560/img/Qnxh33lSvreWzGv6.jpg", "dur": 74}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.17, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112498393956454796", "url": "https://x.com/AiEvolutio58513/status/2112498393956454796", "text": "Sam Altman explains why the AI field, OpenAI included, got jobs wrong:\n\n\"If we could go back to 2019 and show people our latest model, not only would they say that it's AGI, they would say that the economy would have had it completely upended.\"\n\n\"And that has not happened. And I think just from a kind of like intellectual humility point, anytime you're that wrong and that confident, which I think we were as a field, you have to update.\"\n\nWhat he got wrong:\n\n1. \"AI is just very jagged. It's like super human genius in some ways, like dumb toddler in others.\"\n2. \"People have so far extremely complementary skills to AI.\"\n3. \"Somehow most people seem to still really prefer interacting with a human.\"\n\nSame story with coders: \"A year ago, people said software engineers are cooked, it's done, it's over. That didn't happen.\"\n\nEven for his own job, he says people \"don't really want an AI CEO.\"\n\nInterested in AI?\n\nFollow @AiEvolutio58513 and never fall behind.\n\nI track ChatGPT, Claude, and every tool quietly changing how we work and create, then hand you the tested signals.", "name": "AI Evolution", "handle": "AiEvolutio58513", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2051404095026810880/ojNDixza_200x200.png", "likes": 30, "rts": 12, "replies": 2, "views": 2737, "ts": 1792493840, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112498313111248896/vid/avc1/1280x720/XM4Tdnw8JLFtBenS.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112498313111248896/vid/avc1/1920x1080/73P4o53Mmp6PGhLw.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112498313111248896/img/9pOCQkSrAc8jgqn0.jpg", "dur": 83}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.16, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112584064540844143", "url": "https://x.com/graycrawford/status/2112584064540844143", "text": "it appears my squinting simulator is working 👀\n\nwe all love wave optics, naked-eye interference, eyelash diffraction right", "name": "gray ❄️🫧", "handle": "graycrawford", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1704165425355825152/UCBk-jZk_200x200.jpg", "likes": 6831, "rts": 453, "replies": 140, "views": 216881, "ts": 1792514265, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112582325175558147/vid/avc1/1164x720/5beKIYbCg0GgUv-F.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112582325175558147/vid/avc1/3492x2160/lOQTWkhUE1SUs_CB.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112582325175558147/img/luC0N0EWfbn2ldVD.jpg", "dur": 6}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "Everything Else", "score": 5.16, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112501351968055302", "url": "https://x.com/TechCrunch/status/2112501351968055302", "text": "Meeting note-taking tool http://spr.ly/6017BHTo6h announced on Tuesday that it has raised $320 million from General Catalyst’s Customer Value Fund (CVF), which provides capital to startups without diluting equity and gets returns on the results of marketing spend.\nhttp://spr.ly/6019BHToBB", "name": "TechCrunch", "handle": "TechCrunch", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1096066608034918401/m8wnTWsX_200x200.png", "likes": 29, "rts": 4, "replies": 14, "views": 16743, "ts": 1792494545, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Tools & Agents", "score": 5.16, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112279612340232483", "url": "https://x.com/Flandermaxx/status/2112279612340232483", "text": "WHOEVER LEAKED THIS JEV SIGNAL LOOM SHOULD BE WRITING THE WHITE PAPER\n\nI thought asking an agent a question meant prompting the model, waiting for a sentence, and parsing it to figure out what it just said.\n\nApparently not.\n\nThis loom's setup is much more interesting:\n\n→ CHOICE head returns one label from an ordered set in 3ms, nothing else allowed, no free-form string on retry\n→ SCORE head ranks the same set by criterion, one score per item, no \"explain the ranking\" prose anywhere\n→ NOUL head answers yes/no in 4ms with a confidence, below the gate floor drops straight to human review\n→ ONE STATE merges the three heads at 1,257 answers per second, 60 bundles 600 threads, no raw text crosses the gate\n→ CODE acts on the gated state deterministically, flags 5 action drifts above the baseline the author never caught\n\nso you get:\n\nChoices labeled. Scores ranked. Nouls floored. Actions deterministic.\n\nthe interesting part isn't making the model smarter.\nit's giving every question a head whose output type the code can trust.\n\nInstead of parsing one freeform answer per decision at Claude prices, you weave three typed heads at $0.42 per 10,000 decisions, 256ms median, and let the gate drop anything under 0.85.\n\nWeave the heads. Gate the state. Act in code.", "name": "Flandermaxx", "handle": "Flandermaxx", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2096231413234515968/1PYpYwc6_200x200.jpg", "likes": 82, "rts": 13, "replies": 9, "views": 3961, "ts": 1792441678, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112279091944542208/vid/avc1/720x900/NuyRwk-IEdbqwceC.mp4?tag=29", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112279091944542208/vid/avc1/1080x1350/C4E3-CQUK0Ea4R1W.mp4?tag=29", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112279091944542208/img/EnXFKQd6EJexlFL3.jpg", "dur": 27}], "quote": {"id": "2100984487802708306", "url": "https://x.com/0xCodila/status/2100984487802708306", "text": "Jev is the \"Internet\" moment for the AI industry\n\nIt tells your agents and LLMs what to do next, in milliseconds and at almost zero cost\n\nIf you set it up correctly, you will have the AI engineer’s stack for 2028\n\nIn this article, I show you how https://x.com/i/article/2077744776565149697", "name": "codila", "handle": "0xCodila", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2064453666661441536/nj8n8Mei_200x200.jpg", "likes": 3485, "rts": 436, "replies": 94, "views": 2284715, "ts": 1789748710, "media": [], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Models & Labs", "score": 5.16, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}, {"id": "2112596613319537073", "url": "https://x.com/GeniusGTX/status/2112596613319537073", "text": "95% of your B2B market isn't ready to buy right now, and most founders only sell to the other 5%.\n\nAlex Hormozi explained why that leaves most of the money on the table:\n\n\"Let's say 100 people. So you have 100 people and you say, 'Hey, come buy my thing.' Maybe you get one of those people to raise their hand.\"\n\n\"But if we have those same hundred people and we say, 'Hey, you don't have to buy anything. I just want to help you out.' And then after we help them out, we say, 'Hey, now do you want to buy something?' ... we might get three to five times that amount of people.\"\n\n\"You're actually not going to get more traffic. You're just going to convert a higher percentage of it.\"\n\nCame across this article today. Pierre has grown 2 companies to $1M with content and social selling.\n\nHis playbook runs two plans at the same time:\n\n- Passive buyers (95%): open content, a little gated content, and showing up where they already are\n- Active buyers (5%): case studies and demos, warm outbound to anyone who shows a signal, a clear sales process\n- Both lead to a landing page that converts and an entry offer that's easy to say yes to\n\nWorth reading in full:", "name": "GeniusThinking", "handle": "GeniusGTX", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2050658876195065856/wXZMLbh2_200x200.jpg", "likes": 16, "rts": 10, "replies": 2, "views": 3165, "ts": 1792517257, "media": [{"type": "video", "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112596535322296320/vid/avc1/1280x720/ltwgBeYPAv52Vtth.mp4?tag=16", "hd": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2112596535322296320/vid/avc1/1920x1080/p7UyiKQH0ms0_p17.mp4?tag=16", "thumb": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2112596535322296320/img/exfufpc_3YssHvew.jpg", "dur": 99}], "quote": {"id": "2112582208318054427", "url": "https://x.com/PierreHerubel/status/2112582208318054427", "text": "How to actually find B2B clients:\n\nI've grown 2 companies to $1M with content + social selling, including my current agency, ContentPath. Here's the playbook we now run for our B2B clients.\n\nIt's built on one split. About 95% of your market isn't ready to buy right now, and 5% is. You need a plan for both, running in sync:\n\n1/ Passive buyers (95%): get known before they need you\n\nThey're keeping up with their industry and their job. So be the one they learn from:\n\n- Open content for discovery: podcasts, video, and posts from your founder and team\n- Gated content for deeper expertise: webinars, industry reports, a private community. Keep it to about 1% of what you publish, and make it excellent.\n- Social engagement where they already are: events, comments and DMs, outside communities\n\n2/ Active buyers (5%): reach them before a competitor does\n\nBeing ready to buy doesn't mean they'll reach out. So don't wait for them:\n\n- Conversion content to turn your audience into leads: case studies, white papers, demos\n- Warm outbound to start conversations: message anyone who downloads a report, signs up for a webinar or visits your pricing page, and run ABM on your larger accounts. The warmer the signal, the more direct the message.\n- An active sales process to close deals faster: discovery calls, follow-ups by email and DM, a clear closing flow\n\n3/ Both plans lead to 2 things\n\n- A website or landing page that converts\n- An entry offer that's easy to say yes to (build this one first)\n\nB2B founders have paid me to teach them this playbook. Now it's free for everyone in the article below, including how to run it on LinkedIn.\n\n(bookmark for later)", "name": "Pierre", "handle": "PierreHerubel", "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1799519827784036352/QuhIc6Jx_200x200.jpg", "likes": 7, "rts": 3, "replies": 0, "views": 3570, "ts": 1792513822, "media": [{"type": "photo", "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVFmTiOboAESyKM.jpg?name=orig"}], "quote": null, "reply_to": null}, "reply_to": null, "cat": "AI Video, Art & Music", "score": 5.16, "thread": [], "tier": "worth"}]);